# Shell scripts must check out with LF on every platform.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text
# files to CRLF on checkout. For a shell script that is fatal rather than untidy:
# the kernel reads the shebang literally, so `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` sends it
# looking for an interpreter named "bash\r" and the script dies with
# "bad interpreter: no such file or directory" — an error that names the right
# file and says nothing about the carriage return that caused it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the mirror image: keep CRLF, which is what Windows tooling and
# every existing checkout of these files expect.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
